{"answer":"Probably not — ~50% context usage is not a typical "wrap up" threshold, and having pending tasks in the queue is exactly when you want to keep the current session working. The usual pattern is: burn the remaining budget on the queued tasks, and only end (or hand off to a fresh session) when usage approaches the upper bound where compaction kicks in (typically 80–90% of the window), or when the queue is empty. Wrapping up at 50% leaves roughly half the context unused and strands the pending tasks unless they are explicitly handed to a new session.

One legitimate exception: if the remaining tasks are individually heavy — each likely to consume most of a full context on its own — ending now and starting a fresh session per task is the better call. Then "wrap up" is a budget decision, not an early exit.

